 applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: { d: "e" } }, { a: "z", c: { d: null } }); // { a: "z", c: {} }
 ```
+
+## Creating a patch
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` returns a JSON Patch (see above) that turns `from` into `to` when passed to
+`applyPatch`. It describes only what changed: it descends into objects and arrays and emits `add`,
+`remove` and `replace` operations for the differing parts, so identical documents give an empty patch
+and an element inserted in the middle of an array is a single `add`. Neither input is mutated and the
+patch shares no structure with them. It never emits `move`, `copy` or `test`.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+createPatch({ a: 1, b: [1, 2] }, { a: 1, b: [1, 3] }); // [{ op: "replace", path: "/b/1", value: 3 }]
+```
